{"term":"mock","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:660f703095b04aed87","definition":"An imitation, usually of lesser quality.","example":"Is tortured thirst itself too sweet a cup?\nGall, and more bitter mocks, shall make it up.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mock#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:149240494997a34d5d","definition":"Mockery; the act of mocking.","example":"Fooles make a mocke at ſinne: but among the righteous there is fauour.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mock#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:daba796514e4de96da","definition":"Ellipsis of mock examination.","example":"He got a B in his History mock, but improved to an A in the exam.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mock#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f7a28267b72fa59be1","definition":"A mockup or prototype; particularly, ellipsis of mock object, as used in unit testing.","example":"You can, if you must, create a mock that derives from a concrete class. The problem is that the resulting class represents a mix of production and mocked behavior, a beast referred to as a partial mock.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikti